el, CR maintained contractile content and attenuated age-related metabolic shifts among individual fiber types with higher mitochondrial activity, altered redox metabolism, and smaller lipid droplet size. Biometric and metabolic rate data confirm preserved metabolic efficiency in CR animals that correlated with the attenuation of age-related muscle mass and physical activity. These data suggest that CR-induced reprogramming of metabolism plays a role in delayed aging of skeletal muscle in rhesus monkeys.", "affiliation": "Department of Medicine, University of Wisconsin-Madison, Madison, WI 53705, USA.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "BLRD VA", "acronym": "BX", "grantId": "I01 BX003846", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institutes of Health", "grantId": "AG000213", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCRR NIH HHS", "acronym": "RR", "grantId": "C06 RR020141", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCRR NIH HHS", "acronym": "RR", "grantId": "C06 RR015459", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "P01 AG011915", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "R01 AG037000", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "R56 AG047358", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institutes of Health", "grantId": "AG047358", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institutes of Health", "grantId": "AG037000", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "T32 AG000213", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institutes of Health", "grantId": "AG040178", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIDDK NIH HHS", "acronym": "DK", "grantId": "T32 DK007665", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institutes of Health", "grantId": "AG011915", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIH HHS", "acronym": "OD", "grant