nch, National Institute on Aging, Baltimore, Maryland 21224, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Anderson RM", "lastName": "Anderson", "firstName": "Rozalyn M", "initials": "RM", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Medicine, University of Wisconsin, Madison, Wisconsin 53792, USA."}, {"affiliation": "Geriatric Research Education and Clinical Center, William S. Middleton Memorial Veterans Hospital, Madison, Wisconsin 53705, USA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-6511-404X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9706-0525"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0803-1915"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3354-2442"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2830-5693"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data", "wikipedia"]}, "journalInfo": {"volume": "8", "journalIssueId": 2510372, "dateOfPublication": "2017 Jan", "monthOfPublication": 1, "yearOfPublication": 2017, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Nat Commun", "title": "Nature communications", "essn": "2041-1723", "issn": "2041-1723", "nlmid": "101528555", "isoabbreviation": "Nat Commun"}, "printPublicationDate": "2017-01-01"}, "pubYear": "2017", "pageInfo": "14063", "abstractText": "Caloric restriction (CR) without malnutrition extends lifespan and delays the onset of age-related disorders in most species but its impact in nonhuman primates has been controversial. In the late 1980s two parallel studies were initiated to determine the effect of CR in rhesus monkeys. The University of Wisconsin study reported a significant positive impact of CR on survival, but the National Institute on Aging study detected no significant survival effect. Here we present a direct comparison of longitudinal data from both studies including survival, bodyweight, food intake, fasting glucose levels and age-related morbidity. We describe differences in study design that could contribute to differences in outcomes, and we report species specificity in the impact of CR in terms of optimal onset and diet. Taken together these data confirm that health benefits of CR are conserved in monkeys and suggest that CR mechanisms are likely translatable to human health.", "affiliation": "Translational Gerontology Branch, National Institute on Aging, Baltimore, Maryland 21224, USA.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCRR NIH HHS", "acronym": "RR", "grantId": "P51 RR000167", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "R01 AG040178", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIDDK NIH HHS", "acronym": "DK", "grantId": "P30 DK056336", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIH HHS", "acronym": "OD", "grantId": "P51 OD011106", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "R56 AG047358", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "P01 AG011915", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "R01 AG037000", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Animals"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Macaca mulatta", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "GD", "qualifierName": "growth & development"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Body Weight"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Caloric Restriction"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Diet"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Longitudinal Studies"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Energy Intake"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Longevity"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Female"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Male"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms14063"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC5247583"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC5247583?pdf=render"}]}, "isOpenAccess": "Y", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 678, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "N", "hasPDF": "Y", "hasBook": "N", "hasSuppl": "Y", "hasLabsLinks": "Y", "hasData": "Y", "license": "cc by", "authMan": "N", "epmcAuthMan": "N", "nihAuthMan": "N", "hasTMAccessionNumbers": "N", "dateOfCompletion": "2018-11-14", "dateOfCreation": "2017-01-18", "dateOfRevision": "2018-11-14", "electronicPublicationDate": "2017-01-17", "firstPublicationDate": "2017-01-17", "firstIndexDate": "2017-01-18", "fullTextReceivedDate": "2020-07-11", "hasEvaluations": "N"}, {"id": "15604149", "source": "MED", "pmid": "15604149", "pmcid": "PMC539733", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC539733"]}, "doi": "10.1073/pnas.0405831102", "title": "Caloric restriction increases neurotrophic factor levels and attenuates neurochemical and behavioral deficits in a primate model of Parkinson's disease.", "authorString": "Maswood N, Young J, Tilmont E, Zhang Z, Gash DM, Gerhardt GA, Grondin R, Roth GS, Mattison J, Lane MA, Carson RE, Cohen RM, Mouton PR, Quigley C, Mattson MP, Ingram DK.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Maswood N", "lastName": "Maswood", "firstName": "Navin", "initials": "N", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Laboratory of Neurosciences, National Institute on Aging Intramural Research Program, 5600 Nathan Shock Drive, Baltimore, MD 21224, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Young J", "lastName": "Young", "firstName": "Jennifer", "initials": "J"}, {"fullName": "Tilmont E", "lastName": "Tilmont", "firstName": "Edward", "initials": "E"}, {"fullName": "Zhang Z", "lastName": "Zhang", "firstName": "Zhiming", "initials": "Z"}, {"fullName": "Gash DM", "lastName": "Gash", "firstName": "Don M", "initials": "DM"}, {"fullName": "Gerhardt GA", "lastName": "Gerhardt", "firstName": "Greg A", "initials": "GA", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2800-1713"}}, {"fullName": "Grondin R", "lastName": "Grondin", "firstName": "Richard", "initials": "R"}, {"fullName": "Roth GS", "lastName": "Roth", "firstName": "George S", "initials": "GS"}, {"fullName": "Mattison J", "lastName": "Mattison", "firstName": "Julie", "initials": "J"}, {"fullName": "Lane MA", "lastName": "Lane", "firstName": "Mark A", "initials": "MA"}, {"fullName": "Carson RE", "lastName": "Carson", "firstName": "Richard E", "initials": "RE"}, {"fullName": "Cohen RM", "lastName": "Cohen", "firstName": "Robert M", "initials": "RM"}, {"fullName": "Mouton PR", "lastName": "Mouton", "firstName": "Peter R", "initials": "PR"}, {"fullName": "Quigley C", "lastName": "Quigley", "firstName": "Christopher", "initials": "C"}, {"fullName": "Mattson MP", "lastName": "Mattson", "firstName": "Mark P", "initials": "MP"}, {"fullName": "Ingram DK", "lastName": "Ingram", "firstName": "Donald K", "initials": "DK"}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2800-1713"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "52", "volume": "101", "journalIssueId": 1213455, "dateOfPublication": "2004 Dec", "monthOfPublication": 12, "yearOfPublication": 2004, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A", "title": "Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America", "essn": "1091-6490", "issn": "0027-8424", "nlmid": "7505876", "isoabbreviation": "Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A"}, "printPublicationDate": "2004-12-01"}, "pubYear": "2004", "pageInfo": "18171-18176", "abstractText": "We report that a low-calorie diet can lessen the severity of neurochemical deficits and motor dysfunction in a primate model of Parkinson's disease. Adult male rhesus monkeys were maintained for 6 months on a reduced-calorie diet [30% caloric restriction (CR)] or an ad libitum control diet after which they were subjected to treatment with a neurotoxin to produce a hemiparkinson condition. After neurotoxin treatment, CR monkeys exhibited significantly higher levels of locomotor activity compared with control monkeys as well as higher levels of dopamine (DA) and DA metabolites in the striatal region. Increased survival of DA neurons in the substantia nigra and improved manual dexterity were noted but did not reach statistical significance. Levels of glial cell line-derived neurotrophic factor, which is known to promote the survival of DA neurons, were increased significantly in the caudate nucleus of CR monkeys, suggesting a role for glial cell line-derived neurotrophic factor in the anti-Parkinson's disease effect of the low-calorie diet.", "affiliation": "Laboratory of Neurosciences, National Institute on Aging Intramural Research Program, 5600 Nathan Shock Drive, Baltimore, MD 21224, USA.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S.", "research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Brain", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "AH", "qualifierName": "anatomy & histology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Substantia Nigra", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Corpus Striatum", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Neuroglia", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Animals"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Haplorhini"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Macaca mulatta"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Parkinson Disease", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Disease Models, Animal"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Dopamine", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PD", "qualifierName": "pharmacology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "1-Methyl-4-phenyl-1,2,3,6-tetrahydropyridine", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PD", "qualifierName": "pharmacology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Nerve Growth Factors", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "BI", "qualifierName": "biosynthesis"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Brain-Derived Neurotrophic Factor", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "BI", "qualifierName": "biosynthesis"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Neurotrophin 3", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Neurotoxins", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Positron-Emission Tomography